select
  gsm_subject.id, 2016, 2, '2', 'GSM Phone Maintenance & Repair 2016',
  'Question 2
a) List
three
procedures for troubleshooting a faulty mobile phone.
b) Explain each of the procedures listed in 2(a).
Candidates’ performance was poor. This question required the candidates’ knowledge of troubleshooting faulty phones.
.', 'Observation
The expected answers are:
a. Procedures for Troubleshooting
- visualisation;
-knowledge of the phone status;
-software checking;
-analysis of the circuit board.
b. Explanation of Procedures listed in
2
(a)
-Visualisation
- Examine critically the PCB for possible burnt components, corrosion, breakage, dust accumulation etc.
-Knowledge of the Phone status
Ask for the history of the phone from the owner/ user e.g. contact with liquid, frequent falling, wrong insertion/incompatible charger, etc.
-Software checking
Use of flashing device to read the logs of the phone.
