The expected answers are:
Steps required to prevent damage to phone recovered from salty water
Remove the phone immediately from the water;
Ensure it is switched off;
Do not attempt to charge it immediately;
Remove the battery, SIM card, memory card and other accessories;
Attempt to dry the phone partially by dabbing;
Ensure the phone is exposed to dry air for complete dryness before switching it on.
Components that may require attention if phone does not power on
Power IC
PCB
Battery
Battery connector
Actions to be taken on Power IC
Test its status using the multimeter
Replace if faulty
Actions to be taken on PCB
Physical inspection for corrosion
Clean using thinner or PCB cleaner
dry using rework station
Actions to be taken on Battery
Check the terminals for corrosion
Clean terminals if corroded
Check the voltage level using a multimeter
If drained, charge battery
If bad, replace battery
Actions to be taken on Battery connector
Check for corrosion
If corroded, clean
If damaged, replace
